+## A kick of his own, pose to pose, no clip (Sean, 2026-10-24: "a man or the player should be able to
+## kick a chair's legs out"): the knee drawn up, the leg snapped out to `at` and back. The boot is
+## swung by script and meets what's there through the same test as a clip's (`_strike`): a kit
+## prop's member takes the blow its speed gives (KitProp.take_blow decides: it breaks, moves or
+## holds). The angles are worked from where the boot must be: his hip's height over the target's,
+## his leg's length. &"front" drives the boot straight ahead at it; &"sweep" swings it across, from
+## outside in, through it (a chair's two back legs in a line).
+signal kicked(result: StringName)
+## Seconds: drawing the knee up, the snap out, held out, and back. The snap puts the boot through at
+## 9-10 m/s (a hard low kick: a soccer kick's foot runs 15-20, a stamp 5-7), 70-80 N*s from a leg's
+## 8 kg (CLIP_BLOW_MASS): enough to break an oak chair leg and go on into the next.
+const KICK_TIMES := [0.26, 0.05, 0.18, 0.45]
+## Where he stands to kick: his boot (its middle) goes this far through the target at full
+## stretch, so it meets the wood mid-snap at its speed (8-9 m/s); stood so it just reached, it met it
+## as the snap ended, at half that (experiments/physics_lab, 2026-10-24_chair_tip).
+const KICK_THROUGH := 0.12
+## Measured: the middle of his boot at full stretch, short of the hip-to-sole length (m).
+const KICK_SHORT := 0.02
+## A sweep's swing across (s): its whole leg turns, so the same snap would put the boot through at 16.
+const KICK_SWEEP_TIME := 0.1
